# Round 18, C2-15 (follows). L §5.8: "A row x[*] = v states every key of x that exists at the row's known, its own or
# else its version's (§4.6)"; L §4.6 step 1. ks gains c in v2 (known 2026-06-01). x[*] = 1 is known 2026-01-01
# (its version's): it covers a and b, so x[c] is a hole (as L4_6_closed_world). y[*] = 2 states its own known
# 2026-07-01, after c came: it covers c too, y[c] = 2.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ks = [a, b]
input x[k in ks]: int
input y[k in ks]: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x[*] = 1
  y[*] = 2 known 2026-07-01

version v2
  cite s
  known 2026-06-01
  ks + [c]

ask q1: x[a], x[c], y[a], y[c] law 2026-07-01
=== expect
q1: (1, ?"x at c: no value at 2026-07-01" (x[c]), 2, 2)
  law date 2026-07-01, cut 2026-12-31
